/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_Documentation Documentation
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Development
 * @brief Generate the Doxygen HTML site through the normal build workflow.
 *
 * Documentation is configured by the `documentation` preset and built as the
 * CMake `docs` target. It is intentionally kept inside the same preset/script
 * architecture as the library so local development and CI use one command.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowDocsBash Bash
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/docs.sh [preset] [build options]
 *
 * ./scripts/docs.sh
 * ./scripts/docs.sh documentation --fresh --parallel 8
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowDocsPowerShell PowerShell
 *
 * @code{powershell}
 * ./scripts/docs.ps1 [-Preset <preset>] [-Parallel <jobs>] [-Fresh]
 * @endcode
 *
 * The default preset is `documentation`. It enables `FOUNDATION_DOCS`, requires
 * a discoverable Doxygen installation, and builds the `docs` target. Generated
 * HTML is written to:
 *
 * @code
 * build/<preset>/docs/html/index.html
 * @endcode
 *
 * Documentation sources must be registered with `foundation_add_dox()` from a
 * CMakeLists file. Workflow pages are registered by `docs/Workflows/CMakeLists.txt`.
 * Platform pages are registered by `docs/Topics/BuildGuide/CMakeLists.txt`.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowDocsStructure Group Structure
 *
 * Workflow documentation must remain under `docs/Workflows/` and use this
 * hierarchy:
 *
 * @code
 * Workflows
 * |-- Manual Workflow
 * |-- Configuration
 * |   |-- Configure
 * |   |-- Presets
 * |   `-- Toolchains
 * |-- Development
 * |   |-- Build
 * |   |-- Test
 * |   |-- Validation
 * |   |   `-- Windows and macOS Checklist
 * |   |-- Documentation
 * |   `-- Clean
 * `-- Delivery
 *     |-- Install
 *     |-- Export
 *     `-- Precompiled Libraries
 * @endcode
 *
 * Define a page with `@defgroup`, attach it to exactly one subgroup with
 * `@ingroup`, add a concise `@brief`, use globally unique section identifiers,
 * and register the file in the local CMakeLists. Platform-specific integration
 * belongs under Build Guide / Platforms; reusable command behavior belongs here.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowDocsQuality Quality Checks
 *
 * After changing documentation:
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/docs.sh --fresh
 * @endcode
 *
 * Confirm that the command succeeds, the expected group HTML exists, new pages
 * appear below the intended parent, and the output contains no unresolved
 * references, malformed commands, or duplicate section labels. The checked-in
 * configuration intentionally disables `WARN_IF_UNDOCUMENTED`: API coverage is
 * incomplete and is tracked as a separate release task, while structural and
 * semantic documentation errors remain visible. Do not suppress a new warning
 * merely because older public APIs still need descriptions.
 */
